From f882c68d718d0b49fb5496aebb4b787b2316c62a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@local>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 20:20:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] menu: stop gating GPU CONFIG_ACTION on sys-clk availability

Patch 09 added a runtime sys_clk_domain_available() check around
the GPU_PERFPOWER CONFIG_ACTION in menu_setting.c, intending to keep
the entry off the settings tree on builds with no usable GPU. This
broke the Switch GPU menu entirely.

Root cause: the settings tree is built once, at menu_driver_init
time, via menu_setting_new(). retroarch.c::drivers_init() calls
menu_driver_init() before sys_clk_driver_init(), so when the
CONFIG_ACTION runs, sys_clk's GPU drivers list is still NULL and
the guard rejects the entry. Because the settings tree is only
torn down at menu free, the rejection is permanent for the life
of the program - even after sys-clk init runs successfully right
after, the entry is gone for good and any displaylist that tries
to PARSE_ACTION it gets nothing.

This commit reverts the menu_setting.c portion of patch 09: the
GPU_PERFPOWER setting is always registered when HAVE_LAKKA is
defined, matching pre-patch-09 behavior. The runtime guard in
menu_displaylist.c's DISPLAYLIST_POWER_MANAGEMENT_SETTINGS_LIST
case stays - displaylists are rebuilt on every menu navigation,
and by the time the user opens the Power Management page sys-clk
init has long since finished, so the runtime check there is both
correct and effective at hiding the entry on builds with no GPU.

The sys-clk-side changes from patch 09 (sys_clk_domain_available,
the init-time skip of sys_clk_set_mode when drivers is NULL, the
early-outs in set_signal/set_mode) all remain in place; they were
not the cause of the regression.
---
 menu/menu_setting.c | 20 +++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/menu/menu_setting.c b/menu/menu_setting.c
index 9fe9798..68afeb0 100644
--- a/menu/menu_setting.c
+++ b/menu/menu_setting.c
@@ -106,9 +106,6 @@
 #include "../performance_counters.h"
 #include "../setting_list.h"
 #include "../lakka.h"
-#ifdef HAVE_LAKKA
-#include "../misc/sys-clk/sys-clk.h"
-#endif
 #ifdef HAVE_LAKKA_SWITCH
 #include "../lakka-switch.h"
 #endif
@@ -21370,16 +21367,13 @@ static bool setting_append_list(
                parent_group);
 #endif
 #ifdef HAVE_LAKKA
-         /* Only expose the GPU performance entry if the sys-clk
-          * backend found a usable GPU device on this build/host. */
-         if (sys_clk_domain_available(SYS_CLK_DOMAIN_GPU))
-            CONFIG_ACTION(
-                  list, list_info,
-                  MENU_ENUM_LABEL_GPU_PERFPOWER,
-                  MENU_ENUM_LABEL_VALUE_GPU_PERFPOWER,
-                  &group_info,
-                  &subgroup_info,
-                  parent_group);
+         CONFIG_ACTION(
+               list, list_info,
+               MENU_ENUM_LABEL_GPU_PERFPOWER,
+               MENU_ENUM_LABEL_VALUE_GPU_PERFPOWER,
+               &group_info,
+               &subgroup_info,
+               parent_group);
 #endif
 #ifndef HAVE_LAKKA
          if (frontend_driver_has_gamemode())
